From: ruby-edhoc maintainers <ruby-edhoc@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve label-only EAD tokens in message 1

The public EAD callback API represents a label-only token with a NULL value
pointer. Message 1 unconditionally marked the value present, serializing a
zero-length byte string instead of omitting the value.

diff --git a/library/core/edhoc_message_1.c b/library/core/edhoc_message_1.c
--- a/library/core/edhoc_message_1.c
+++ b/library/core/edhoc_message_1.c
@@ -207,7 +207,8 @@ int edhoc_message_1_compose(struct edhoc_context *ctx,
 
 		for (size_t i = 0; i < ctx->ead.count; ++i) {
 			cbor_enc_msg_1.message_1_EAD_1_m.EAD_1[i]
-				.ead_x_ead_value_present = true;
+				.ead_x_ead_value_present =
+				(NULL != ctx->ead.token[i].value.value);
 			cbor_enc_msg_1.message_1_EAD_1_m.EAD_1[i]
 				.ead_x_ead_label = ctx->ead.token[i].label;
 			cbor_enc_msg_1.message_1_EAD_1_m.EAD_1[i]
